<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="622a6093-3743-5f94-a19f-2532fc24ca35" activityNameId="1a239757-c212-52b6-9ecd-4cc278e98cd3" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Neodymium oxide, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Neodymium oxide, at plant
In- and outputs are calculated for rare earth oxide processing with sulphuric acid as used in China. Infrastructure approximated with a chemical plant. Some inputs of auxiliary materials are calculated according to stoechiometry. Rough estimation for energy consumption, solvent use and waste generation.;
UUID: 13a46619-2c77-36a1-90cd-df7121eed9c5
The process includes raw materials, processing chemicals and processing energy, emissions to water and wastes. Transport and infrastructure are estimated. The multi output-process "rare earth oxide production from bastnasite" delivers the co-products "cerium concentrate, 60% cerium oxide, at plant", "lanthanum oxide, at plant", "neodymium oxide, at plant","praseodymium oxide, at plant", "samarium europium gadolinium concentrate 94% rare earth oxide, at plant". The revenue is used as allocation scheme.
Location: Production in China considered. Process applicable for other regions if a similar process is used.
Technology: Process includes roasting and cracking of the rare earth concentrate with 98% sulphuric acid at 500°C in a rotary kiln. For the following separation of the different rare earth oxides solvent extraction (SX) is used. The obtained rare earth oxide product has a purity of up to 99.9%.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: based on literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_13a46619-2c77-36a1-90cd-df7121eed9c5.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="3142d8e2-0d30-557e-b090-9faae2b72357" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">CN</shortname>
